  "name": "Sunbeam hall",
  "description": "Greybox reference puzzle for light (mw-e15.9): a shaft of sunlight shines north from the south-west corner of a 10 m hall; two mirror stands, turned with Interact, can carry it east and north to a beam sensor by the north-east wall, and a brazier stands beside the sensor. When the sensor is lit, or the brazier burns, for a second the puzzle sunbeam-hall is solved and the portcullis to the north rises. The beam is not the only way: a burning barrel waits by the south wall for anyone willing to carry flame to the brazier, and a fire spell (Ember) lights it from across the room. Reach it with ?scene=sunbeam-hall.",
